    <h2 class="section-title">Dark matter to launch hardware.</h2>

    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-text">
        <p>
          I'm Jacob. I work at <strong>Blue Origin</strong> in Kent, WA on the software that runs avionics
          verification for New Glenn and other programs - the testing infrastructure between the engineers
          and the flight hardware.
        </p>
        <p>
          Physics undergrad at Florida Tech, particle research at <strong>CERN</strong>, then HPC
          scientific software at ENSCO before moving to aerospace. The common thread has been making
          computation fast and correct when the stakes are high.
        </p>
        <p>
          I've also spent a lot of time running organizations - student government, LGBTQ+ groups,
          fraternity boards. That side of things taught me things about people that no amount of
          code review does.
        </p>
        <div class="about-tags">
          <span class="tag">aerospace</span>
          <span class="tag">avionics</span>
          <span class="tag">particle physics</span>
          <span class="tag">quantum computing</span>
          <span class="tag">HPC</span>
          <span class="tag">DEI</span>
          <span class="tag">open source</span>
          <span class="tag">scientific computing</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="about-interests">
        <h3>Research &amp; Interests</h3>
